 kit packages - lists the packages in reach, and changes which are active

   one of
   *kit packages*              lists the packages in reach, and changes which are active

     --active   --inactive   only the active packages

     --text   --json   --jq  lists the packages as text, even on a terminal; with packages, the
                             stage as a table

     <package>…              a name, such as style/bash, or a glob, such as 'style/*'

   (select | add | remove) <package>
   --stages                  prints the stages, one per line: packages
   --marks                   prints the stage's mark, as one JSON object, which changes when kit.yml
                             or .kit/packages/ does
   packages                  the stage: a row per package in reach, {name, state, origin, depends,
                             includes, dependents, bundles, description}, keyed by its name;
                             dependents are the active packages that depend on it, and bundles the
                             active ones that include it


 kit packages
